body:
vcodecd must (a) bring the guest set up on the fake/real n2vc_hw, (b) get the struct n2vcu* that V41s n2ap_venc_open takes, (c) detect a guest stop between requests for the watchdog and report its detail. I propose exactly this, and I am coding against it behind daemon/n2ip_deps.h until host/n2vhost.h lands:

  struct n2vhost;
  int  n2vhost_start(struct n2vhost **out, const struct n2vc_hw *hw, const char *vendor_dir);
  struct n2vcu *n2vhost_vcu(struct n2vhost *vh);
  int  n2vhost_stop_reason(struct n2vhost *vh);     /* 0 = guest still running; else n2a32 stop code (U DEF/FAULT/NOIMPORT/...) or -errno if the host thread died */
  const char *n2vhost_detail(struct n2vhost *vh);   /* one line: "UNDEF at pc=0x... thumb", "missing import <name> at ...", "fault at ..."; never NULL */
  void n2vhost_stop(struct n2vhost *vh);

n2vhost_stop_reason() is polled every 100 ms by the daemon loop (no blocking) and read after every n2ap_venc call. If you prefer one call `int n2vhost_status(struct n2vhost *, const char **detail)`, fine - tell me the final name/signature and I will change one file. If guest threads continue after a stop_request is observed, say so: the daemon tears down and calls n2vhost_stop() only at process exit in v1 (a stop is fatal for the whole hosted set until restart), and I would rather not free guest memory under a live thread.

Also: does n2vhost_start() return before or after M-a/M-b (link + init arrays)? vcodecd can accept "not ready yet" and answer OPEN with E_HW (not crash), so either is fine - tell me which error code means "vendor set absent" vs "bring-up failed" so OPEN can map them.
No phone work in my package; tests use the fake n2vc_hw only.
